Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:49:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] Anticheat: BO2's code checks (push type 19), judged
 against the host's own answers

The server pushes code-checksum challenges (CRC-32 of game code ranges) to every player and compares the answers
with the session host's (DW_TRUSTED_USER) on the same build; a player whose answers differ runs changed game
code and their sessions are refused. Verified on BO2 1.19 (PS3): the launcher and multiplayer answers match
CRCs computed from the decrypted executables. The push goes to the player's PS3 user id (Tiger hash of the
online ID); any other id hits a log line that crashes the game. Lobby servers can now send push messages after
a reply (PushSource).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
