+//! Anticheat (service 38), Black Ops II style: the server pushes challenges (push type 19) and the game answers
+//! them with AnswerChallenges. Reversed from BO2 1.19 (PS3, `live/live_anticheat_mipster.cpp`):
+//!
+//! - Push: `u32 19, u64 user id, string (<= 64), u16 count, count x { u16 type, u64 id, u16 n, n x blob }`.
+//! - Type 1 (what we send): CRC-32 of a range of the game's own code. Blob: `u64 key, i64 start, i64 end,
+//!   u8 len + module name, u8 len + section name` (big endian). An empty module is the main executable; start and
+//!   end are offsets from its start (clamped to it). The CRC uses the reflected 0xEDB88320 table, starts from the
+//!   key's low 32 bits and has no final xor.
+//! - AnswerChallenges (task 2): `u16 count, count x { u64 id, i64 answer }, blob (<= 64, game info)`. The
+//!   blob starts with the executable's build (`[1][u32 build][u8]`): the launcher and multiplayer are different
+//!   code, so answers are only compared between players on the same build.
+//!
+//! Players don't have a decrypted copy of the game to work answers out from, so the reference is the session
